WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.750
Well we’re all very excited to have you here

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.833
But I must warn you, the Garpax has eyes EVERYWHERE

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:17.083
Be careful what you say

00:00:17.291 --> 00:00:18.791
and let your game do the talking

00:00:19.041 --> 00:00:19.958
Have no doubt,

00:00:19.958 --> 00:00:23.000
I’m as healthy as ever AND I shoot threes now

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.125
There’s no reason we can’t form a superteam

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.250
Is that...is that  Dwyane Wade?
—here in Chicago—

00:00:27.666 --> 00:00:29.500
Oh Seven Hells

00:00:29.541 --> 00:00:31.833
It is. It is you!

00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:32.833
Who is that?

00:00:32.875 --> 00:00:33.875
Someone you know?

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:34.750
Mario Chalmers

00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.208
We used to play together in Miami

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.916
Oh great, here we go

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:40.125
Hello Rio

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:41.708
Nooooo

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.125
You’re on the Bulls now?

00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:46.708
Oh that’s so WEIRD

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:49.041
We was on a superteam together

00:00:49.708 --> 00:00:50.708
“The Big Four!”

00:00:51.041 --> 00:00:52.458
‘Member those days, Dwyane?

00:00:52.666 --> 00:00:53.375
...no?

00:00:53.375 --> 00:00:55.125
But I can’t blame you for leaving really

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:56.500
Twilight-a your career...

00:00:56.541 --> 00:00:58.416
bad knees, bad shoulders...

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.333
maybe you can scrape together one last playoff run with...

00:01:01.791 --> 00:01:02.791
sorry what’s your name?

00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:04.458
Jimmy Butler

00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:05.916
Oh

00:01:06.208 --> 00:01:08.291
You DO look a lot like Michael Jordan

00:01:08.291 --> 00:01:10.375
Well it’s all very exciting

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:12.083
We must be going now, I’m afraid

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.166
Oh. Alright, um, well,

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:15.208
if you need a point guard

00:01:15.958 --> 00:01:16.916
or whatever...

00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:16.958
or whatever...
just, send me a raven, yeah?

00:01:16.958 --> 00:01:18.333
just, send me a raven, yeah?

00:01:18.333 --> 00:01:19.291
We have Rondo

00:01:19.291 --> 00:01:20.208
Oh well,

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:21.333
you never know with him

00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:22.416
He’s a bit...

00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:23.375
(crazy whistle)

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:25.875
You’ll definitely need a veteran backup, no?

00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:29.125
We have plenty of depth but we’ll keep you in mind

00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:30.125
Cause...you know,

00:01:30.166 --> 00:01:31.916
we could be a superteam again!

00:01:32.083 --> 00:01:33.208
Bye Rio!

00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:35.625
YOU CAN YELL AT ME ALL YOU LIKE

00:01:35.666 --> 00:01:36.666
I DON’T MIND!

00:01:38.416 --> 00:01:39.791
Alright, well...

00:01:41.125 --> 00:01:42.416
guess I’ll head to Cleveland

00:01:57.375 --> 00:01:58.416
Gadzooks!

00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:00.083
Come in, come in!

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:05.916
I came to say hello and welcome you to Houston

00:02:05.916 --> 00:02:07.208
Ah! Why thank you!

00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:09.375
And you must be the new scouting apprentice!

00:02:09.375 --> 00:02:10.541
I’ve been expecting you

00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:13.833
Uh...I’m your starting shooting guard...

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.240
James Harden?

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.460
All Realm shooting guard?

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.208
James... James... you say...

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:23.208
one moment please!
&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;font color=#00000000&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:29.458 --> 00:02:30.291
Aha!

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.625
James Harden!

00:02:31.625 --> 00:02:33.750
The point guard. Forgive me.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:34.291
Shooting guard--

00:02:34.291 --> 00:02:36.000
I’ve been studying your game...

00:02:36.125 --> 00:02:38.916
it’s marvelous. Brilliant really!

00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:42.000
Oh, that’s very kind of you to say...

00:02:43.166 --> 00:02:45.916
So you...have a lot of books, I see

00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:49.041
This whole shelf is... inbound plays?

00:02:49.041 --> 00:02:49.541
Ah yes...

00:02:49.625 --> 00:02:50.916
baseline, sideline...

00:02:51.166 --> 00:02:53.166
I also keep iso plays in there somewhere

00:02:53.291 --> 00:02:54.708
for no good reason really

00:02:54.708 --> 00:02:56.041
And this shelf here,

00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:58.583
all books on the art of the pass

00:02:58.583 --> 00:02:59.125
Wow!

00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:02.333
Over there, that's tempo plays, pick and rolls...

00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:03.333
you name it!

00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:05.333
Feel free to borrow them as you please, by the way

00:03:05.333 --> 00:03:06.041
Wow

00:03:06.041 --> 00:03:08.750
I bet you need whole new library just for all

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:09.708
defensive plays

00:03:10.708 --> 00:03:11.333
Hmm?

00:03:12.833 --> 00:03:14.583
Defense...like...you know

00:03:14.625 --> 00:03:17.166
when the other team has the ball?

00:03:17.208 --> 00:03:19.458
...And they try to...you know...score...

00:03:19.458 --> 00:03:20.875
on... us?

00:03:20.916 --> 00:03:23.291
Oh no no no. None of that here

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:25.333
It’s a waste of energy and it’s no fun

00:03:25.708 --> 00:03:26.541
I say

00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:28.125
half the defense...

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:31.083
double the offense!

